  "body": "Currently [spec says](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#preprocessing-the-input-stream):\r\n> Any occurrences of surrogates, noncharacters, or controls other than ASCII whitespace are parse errors.\r\n\r\nHowever, if surrogates are in a pair they form perfectly valid unicode character. Therefore is should be `Any occurrences of isolated surrogates`. Moreover, tests currently don't treat surrogate pairs as errors, e.g.: https://github.com/html5lib/html5lib-tests/blob/master/tokenizer/unicodeChars.test#L1287.  ",
